---
/**
 * EnterHelmBoard.astro
 * Opening view: "Enter Helm: Three Roles & The Scenarios It Covers"
 * Showcases the 3 distinct hats Helm wears in modern DevOps workflows,
 * the persistent scenario (payment-api umbrella stack), and the map of scenarios covered.
 */
---
<div class="helm-enter-board" data-helm-enter-board>
  <div class="helm-enter-hero">
    <div class="helm-hats-grid">
      <!-- Role 1 -->
      <div class="helm-hat-card is-template">
        <div class="helm-hat-header">
          <span class="helm-hat-num">ROLE 01</span>
          <h4>Template Engine</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="helm-hat-desc">
          Compiles parameterized values and Go templates into raw, multi-document Kubernetes YAML.
        </p>
        <ul class="helm-hat-details">
          <li><strong>Zero Cluster Mutation:</strong> Runs completely offline on local machines or CI runners.</li>
          <li><strong>GitOps Engine:</strong> Argo CD uses <code>helm template</code> to generate manifests before applying them.</li>
          <li><strong>Security & Linting:</strong> Feeds generated manifests to scanners like Trivy, Checkov, or OPA Gatekeeper.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="helm-hat-commands">
          <code>helm template</code>
          <code>helm lint</code>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Role 2 -->
      <div class="helm-hat-card is-package">
        <div class="helm-hat-header">
          <span class="helm-hat-num">ROLE 02</span>
          <h4>Package & Artifact Manager</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="helm-hat-desc">
          Fetches, packages, versions, and cryptographically verifies chart archives (.tgz) from HTTP or OCI registries.
        </p>
        <ul class="helm-hat-details">
          <li><strong>OCI Standard:</strong> Distributes charts as first-class container artifacts to GHCR, ECR, Harbor.</li>
          <li><strong>Supply Chain Security:</strong> Validates digital provenance signatures (<code>--verify</code>) before saving.</li>
          <li><strong>Air-Gapped Workflows:</strong> Relays third-party vendor charts into private internal networks.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="helm-hat-commands">
          <code>helm pull</code>
          <code>helm package</code>
          <code>helm push</code>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Role 3 -->
      <div class="helm-hat-card is-release">
        <div class="helm-hat-header">
          <span class="helm-hat-num">ROLE 03</span>
          <h4>Cluster Release Manager</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="helm-hat-desc">
          Communicates with the Kubernetes API, tracks release revisions in cluster secrets, executes lifecycle hooks, and manages rollbacks.
        </p>
        <ul class="helm-hat-details">
          <li><strong>In-Cluster State:</strong> Records each deploy as a revision Secret (<code>sh.helm.release.v1.*</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>Transactional Safety:</strong> Executes pre/post migration hooks and enforces readiness timeouts.</li>
          <li><strong>Atomic Rollbacks:</strong> Reverts failing upgrades back to the previous stable release.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="helm-hat-commands">
          <code>helm upgrade -i</code>
          <code>helm rollback</code>
          <code>helm status</code>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Persistent Scenario & Journey Map -->
  <div class="helm-scenario-showcase">
    <div class="helm-scenario-banner">
      <div class="helm-scenario-main">
        <span class="helm-scenario-tag">PERSISTENT WORKLOAD SCENARIO</span>
        <h3>The <code>payment-api</code> Umbrella Stack</h3>
        <p>
          Throughout this console, you follow a single real-world production service: an umbrella chart combining your core <strong>payment-api</strong> deployment, an aliased <strong>cache</strong> (from Redis), an embedded <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> database, and an enterprise <strong>common-templates</strong> library chart.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="helm-scenario-stats">
        <div class="stat-item"><span>CHART VERSION</span><strong>1.2.0</strong></div>
        <div class="stat-item"><span>APP VERSION</span><strong>4.7.1</strong></div>
        <div class="stat-item"><span>NAMESPACE</span><strong>payments</strong></div>
        <div class="stat-item"><span>RELEASE STATUS</span><strong>rev 2 (deployed)</strong></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Scenarios Covered Map -->
    <div class="helm-covered-map">
      <div class="map-section-title">ROADMAP: SCENARIOS COVERED ACROSS THIS CONSOLE</div>
      <div class="map-grid">
        <div class="map-node">
          <span class="step-num">01–04</span>
          <strong>Local Compilation</strong>
          <p>Chart file anatomy, values precedence, map vs list replacement, and offline rendering capabilities.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="map-node">
          <span class="step-num">05–08</span>
          <strong>Umbrella Composition</strong>
          <p>Declaring dependencies, condition vs alias gotchas, scoped child values, Chart.lock reproducibility, and library charts.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="map-node">
          <span class="step-num">09</span>
          <strong>Artifact Lifecycle</strong>
          <p>Packaging <code>.tgz</code> archives, pushing to modern OCI registries, pulling, and verifying provenance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="map-node">
          <span class="step-num">10–13</span>
          <strong>Cluster Release Transactions</strong>
          <p>Release secret ledgers, <code>upgrade --install</code> lifecycle, hook execution, and simulating failed rollout rollbacks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="map-node">
          <span class="step-num">14–16</span>
          <strong>Production Delivery</strong>
          <p>Comparing legacy CI push against GitOps (Argo CD vs Flux), handling manual drift, and the 6-step change loop.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
.helm-enter-board {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.25rem;
  background: var(--surface-bg, #161a22);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, #30363d);
  border-radius: 8px;
}
.helm-hats-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 1rem;
}
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .helm-hats-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
.helm-hat-card {
  background: var(--layer-bg, #0d1117);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, #30363d);
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 1rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.65rem;
  position: relative;
  border-top: 3px solid #58a6ff;
}
.helm-hat-card.is-template { border-top-color: #388bfd; }
.helm-hat-card.is-package { border-top-color: #d29922; }
.helm-hat-card.is-release { border-top-color: #7ee787; }

.helm-hat-header {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.2rem;
}
.helm-hat-num {
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  color: var(--text-muted, #8b949e);
}
.helm-hat-header h4 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  color: #f0f6fc;
}
.helm-hat-desc {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 0.825rem;
  color: #c9d1d9;
  line-height: 1.4;
}
.helm-hat-details {
  margin: 0;
  padding-left: 1.1rem;
  font-size: 0.775rem;
  color: #8b949e;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}
.helm-hat-details li strong {
  color: #e6edf3;
}
.helm-hat-commands {
  margin-top: auto;
  padding-top: 0.5rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}
.helm-hat-commands code {
  background: #21262d;
  color: #79c0ff;
  padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
  border-radius: 4px;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  border: 1px solid #30363d;
}

.helm-scenario-showcase {
  background: #0d1117;
  border: 1px solid #30363d;
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 1.1rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1.25rem;
}
.helm-scenario-banner {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 1.5rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;
  padding-bottom: 1rem;
}
@media (max-width: 820px) {
  .helm-scenario-banner {
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}
.helm-scenario-main {
  flex: 1;
}
.helm-scenario-tag {
  font-size: 0.675rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  color: #58a6ff;
  display: inline-block;
  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
}
.helm-scenario-main h3 {
  margin: 0 0 0.35rem 0;
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  color: #f0f6fc;
}
.helm-scenario-main p {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 0.825rem;
  color: #8b949e;
  line-height: 1.45;
}
.helm-scenario-main p strong {
  color: #e6edf3;
}
.helm-scenario-stats {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
  background: #161b22;
  border: 1px solid #30363d;
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
}
.stat-item {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.15rem;
}
.stat-item span {
  font-size: 0.65rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #8b949e;
}
.stat-item strong {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: #7ee787;
  font-family: monospace;
}

.map-section-title {
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  color: #8b949e;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
.map-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
  gap: 0.6rem;
}
@media (max-width: 980px) {
  .map-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }
}
@media (max-width: 580px) {
  .map-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
.map-node {
  background: #161b22;
  border: 1px solid #30363d;
  border-radius: 5px;
  padding: 0.65rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}
.map-node .step-num {
  font-size: 0.65rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #58a6ff;
  font-family: monospace;
}
.map-node strong {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: #f0f6fc;
}
.map-node p {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 0.725rem;
  color: #8b949e;
  line-height: 1.35;
}
</style>
